      "math_academy_id": "e-9400",
      "problem": "Calculate the value of $\\dfrac{1}{4} - \\dfrac{5}{6}.$",
      "worked_solution": "We write $\\dfrac{1}{4}$ as $\\dfrac{3}{12}$ and $\\dfrac{5}{6}$ as $\\dfrac{10}{12},$ and then we simply subtract the numerators. This gives\n\n$$\n\\dfrac{3}{12} - \\dfrac{10}{12} = \\dfrac{3 - 10}{12}.\n$$\n\nNow, we work out $3 - 10$ using a number line:\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/linear/14148354/assets/f4dc7569aa731c13cf150d867479704cc46cbf7d6502cda4100538b4b2a7e9dc.png)\n\nSo, we get\n\n$$\n\\dfrac{3 - 10}{12} = \\dfrac{-7}{12} = -\\dfrac{7}{12}.\n$$",
